00:05:55.230 --> 00:05:57.492
Well, so what is ML Kit?

00:05:57.492 --> 00:05:58.450
BRAHIM ELBOUCHIKHI: OK.

00:05:58.450 --> 00:06:00.640
So, ML Kit is essentially
Google's machine

00:06:00.640 --> 00:06:04.760
learning SDK, available through
Firebase-- integrated deeply

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:05.930
into Firebase.

00:06:05.930 --> 00:06:08.430
It offers a couple
of capabilities.

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:10.520
One is what we call Base APIs.

00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:13.150
These are APIs that essentially
allow you to do stuff--

00:06:13.150 --> 00:06:15.070
you get an input and
you get an output.

00:06:15.070 --> 00:06:17.570
There is, essentially, as far
as the developer is concerned,

00:06:17.570 --> 00:06:19.430
no machine learning involved.

00:06:19.430 --> 00:06:21.740
Google provides the
machine learning models

00:06:21.740 --> 00:06:24.180
and makes them available
through a simple API.

00:06:24.180 --> 00:06:25.410
So that's one set of things.

00:06:25.410 --> 00:06:27.890
And then the other
aspect is essentially

00:06:27.890 --> 00:06:30.380
enabling developers to use
their own custom models

00:06:30.380 --> 00:06:32.541
and making that as
easy as possible.

00:06:32.541 --> 00:06:34.790
That is something that Sachin
is deeply familiar with,

00:06:34.790 --> 00:06:36.890
so I'm going to maybe ask
you to jump in and talk

00:06:36.890 --> 00:06:38.016
a bit about that, Sachin.

00:06:38.016 --> 00:06:38.890
SACHIN KOTWANI: Sure.

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:40.760
Brahim, before I jump
into that, I actually

00:06:40.760 --> 00:06:43.500
also want to talk about one
cool thing about Base APIs--

00:06:43.500 --> 00:06:46.400
that I think it's a very
interesting and different

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:49.840
from what we've seen
thus far in this space--

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:54.620
is that ML Kit offers APIs that
run both on-device or in-cloud.

00:06:54.620 --> 00:06:57.200
And depending on the
functionality you want to use,

00:06:57.200 --> 00:06:59.919
some APIs are available
to run fully on-device.

00:06:59.919 --> 00:07:01.460
Some are only
available in the cloud,

00:07:01.460 --> 00:07:03.856
and some offer the option
of using one or the other.

00:07:03.856 --> 00:07:06.230
And of course, if you want to
do something more powerful,

00:07:06.230 --> 00:07:08.294
the capabilities will be
there in the cloud API,

00:07:08.294 --> 00:07:09.960
but if you want to
do something locally,

00:07:09.960 --> 00:07:11.580
you could do that on-device.

00:07:11.580 --> 00:07:14.000
Now, for the custom models--

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:16.650
if you are an expert
in machine learning,

00:07:16.650 --> 00:07:19.250
you know ML Kit first and
foremost positions itself

00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:21.980
as a tool that makes
it very easy to bring

00:07:21.980 --> 00:07:23.244
machine learning to your apps.

00:07:23.244 --> 00:07:25.160
But if you're already
familiar with TensorFlow

00:07:25.160 --> 00:07:27.290
and creating your
own models, you

00:07:27.290 --> 00:07:32.210
can also use ML Kit to
deliver those models

00:07:32.210 --> 00:07:33.770
to your developers.

00:07:33.770 --> 00:07:35.990
And you would upload
your custom model

00:07:35.990 --> 00:07:39.320
and it would be seamlessly
deployed to the user's device

00:07:39.320 --> 00:07:42.140
without them having to
download anything manually.

00:07:42.140 --> 00:07:44.120
So that infrastructure
piece is taken care of.

00:07:44.120 --> 00:07:45.840
We are just getting
started there.

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:47.889
There's a lot more to
come in the near future,

00:07:47.889 --> 00:07:49.430
but that's an area
that we are really

00:07:49.430 --> 00:07:50.540
passionate about as well.

